"affinity of all unbound workqueues.  This function check the **cpumask** and "
"apply it to all unbound workqueues and updates all pwqs of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7810
msgid ""
"0       - Success -EINVAL - Invalid **cpumask** -ENOMEM - Failed to allocate "
"memory for attrs or pwqs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7908
msgid "make a workqueue visible in sysfs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7909
msgid "the workqueue to register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7910
msgid ""
"Expose **wq** in sysfs under /sys/bus/workqueue/devices. alloc_workqueue*() "
"automatically calls this function if WQ_SYSFS is set which is the preferred "
"method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7914
msgid ""
"Workqueue user should use this function directly iff it wants to apply "
"workqueue_attrs before making the workqueue visible in sysfs; otherwise, "
"apply_workqueue_attrs() may race against userland updating the attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7968
msgid "undo workqueue_sysfs_register()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7969
msgid "the workqueue to unregister"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:7970
msgid ""
"If **wq** is registered to sysfs by workqueue_sysfs_register(), unregister."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8348
msgid "early init for workqueue subsystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8349
msgid ""
"This is the first step of three-staged workqueue subsystem initialization "
"and invoked as soon as the bare basics - memory allocation, cpumasks and idr "
"are up. It sets up all the data structures and system workqueues and allows "
"early boot code to create workqueues and queue/cancel work items. Actual "
"work item execution starts only after kthreads can be created and scheduled "
"right before early initcalls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8487
msgid "bring workqueue subsystem fully online"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8488
msgid ""
"This is the second step of three-staged workqueue subsystem initialization "
"and invoked as soon as kthreads can be created and scheduled. Workqueues "
"have been created and work items queued on them, but there are no kworkers "
"executing the work items yet. Populate the worker pools with the initial "
"workers and enable future kworker creations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8610
msgid "count distinct cores (SMT groups) within an LLC pod"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8616
#: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8695
msgid "``const struct cpumask *pod_cpus``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8611
#: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8690
msgid "the cpumask of CPUs in the LLC pod"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8613
#: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8692
msgid "``struct wq_pod_type *smt_pods``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8612
#: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8691
msgid "the SMT pod type, used to identify sibling groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8613
msgid ""
"A core is represented by the lowest-numbered CPU in its SMT group. Returns "
"the number of distinct cores found in **pod_cpus**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8689
msgid "populate cpu_shard_id[] for each CPU in an LLC pod"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8693
msgid "``int nr_cores``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8692
msgid "number of distinct cores in **pod_cpus** (from llc_count_cores())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8693
msgid ""
"Walks **pod_cpus** in order. At each SMT group leader, advances to the next "
"shard once the current shard is full. Results are written to cpu_shard_id[]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8744
msgid "assign each CPU its shard index within its LLC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8745
msgid ""
"Iterates over all LLC pods. For each pod, counts distinct cores then assigns "
"shard indices to all CPUs in the pod. Must be called after WQ_AFFN_CACHE and "
"WQ_AFFN_SMT have been initialized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8787
msgid "initialize CPU pods for unbound workqueues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/workqueue:795: ../kernel/workqueue.c:8788
msgid ""
"This is the third step of three-staged workqueue subsystem initialization "
"and invoked after SMP and topology information are fully initialized. It "
"initializes the unbound CPU pods accordingly."
msgstr ""
